{"version": 2, "width": 110, "height": 40, "timestamp": 1790279008, "title": "Laplace: a heisenbug recorded in the booted OS, debugged backward over MCP and gdb", "env": {"TERM": "xterm-256color", "SHELL": "/bin/bash"}}
[0.0, "o", "$ python3 tests/qemu/timetravel_e2e.py\r\n"]
[0.169615, "o", "=== Laplace: a heisenbug recorded in the booted OS, debugged backward ===\r\n[boot] QEMU: IDE disk, console on COM1, gdb on :41231 (COM2), MCP on :34193 (COM3)\r\n"]
[0.67276, "o", "  [ok] the machine stopped for the debugger\r\n[run ] break: pid 1 asserted (code bad) at epoch 1, step 679\r\n  [ok] the heisenbug's assertion fired (code 0xbad)\r\n\r\n[mcp ] an agent attaches through tools/laplace-mcp\r\n"]
[0.810161, "o", "  [ok] initialize handshake\r\n"]
[0.935677, "o", "  [ok] tools/list: 13 tools with input schemas\r\n"]
[0.980193, "o", "  mcp> where()\r\n       position epoch=1 offset=679 insn=0 pid=1 rip=0x400001e1 stop=break: pid 1 asserted (code bad) (end of the recording)\r\n  [ok] positioned at the end of the recording\r\n"]
[1.023363, "o", "  mcp> list_processes()\r\n       pid=1 name=heisenbug current\r\npid=2 name=noise\r\npid=3 name=noise\r\n"]
[1.068477, "o", "  mcp> read_memory(pid=1, addr=0x40001100, len=4)\r\n       pid=1 addr=0x40001100 len=4 bytes=b49f0000 u32=40884\r\n"]
[1.068962, "o", "  [ok] batch_limit is 40884, not 48: clobbered\r\n\r\n[mcp ] who wrote batch_limit last?\r\n"]
[1.446489, "o", "  mcp> watch_last_write(pid=1, addr=0x40001100, len=4)\r\n       last write at epoch=1 offset=662 insn=26 pid=1 rip=0x400000b3\r\n  [ok] watch_last_write found the write\r\n"]
[1.447111, "o", "  [ok] landed right after the store in produce() (0x400000b3)\r\n"]
[1.49033, "o", "  mcp> get_registers(pid=1)\r\n       pid=1 rax=0x40 rbx=0x7fffff98 rcx=0x9f74 rdx=0x38 rsi=0x1 rdi=0x9fb4 rbp=0x7fffffe0 rsp=0x7fffff58 r8=0x28972228 r9=0xcccccccccccccccd r10=0x38 r11=0x37 r12=0x7fffff64 r13=0x7fffff80 r14=0x0 r15=0x0 rip=0x400000b3 rflags=0x200\r\n"]
[1.491091, "o", "  [ok] rax (the slot index) is 64: one past a 64-slot ring\r\n"]
[1.533183, "o", "  mcp> read_memory(pid=1, addr=0x40001100, len=4)\r\n       pid=1 addr=0x40001100 len=4 bytes=b49f0000 u32=40884\r\n  [ok] the value there is the clobbered one\r\n"]
[1.680428, "o", "  mcp> reverse_stepi()\r\n       now at epoch=1 offset=662 insn=25 pid=1 rip=0x400000ac\r\n"]
[1.680515, "o", "  [ok] one instruction back is the store (0x400000ac)\r\n"]
[1.723508, "o", "  mcp> read_memory(pid=1, addr=0x40001100, len=4)\r\n       pid=1 addr=0x40001100 len=4 bytes=30000000 u32=48\r\n  [ok] before the store, batch_limit was still 48\r\n"]
[1.7664, "o", "  mcp> stepi()\r\n       now at epoch=1 offset=662 insn=26 pid=1 rip=0x400000b3\r\n  [ok] stepi forward re-executes the store\r\n"]
[1.922296, "o", "  mcp> verify_replay()\r\n       byte-exact: epochs_checked=1 epochs_diverged=0\r\n"]
[1.923075, "o", "  [ok] every retained epoch (1) re-executes byte-exact\r\n\r\n[gdb ] stock gdb attaches to the same machine\r\n"]
[5.260606, "o", "  gdb> main () at user/laplace/heisenbug.c:73\r\n  gdb> 73\t        if (iter % 4096 == 0) {\r\n  gdb> $1 = 40884\r\n  gdb> Hardware watchpoint 1: -location g.batch_limit\r\n  gdb> Thread 1 hit Hardware watchpoint 1: -location g.batch_limit\r\n  gdb> Old value = 40884\r\n  gdb> New value = 48\r\n  gdb> 0x00000000400000ac in produce (payload=payload@entry=40884, burst=burst@entry=1) at user/laplace/heisenbug.c:42\r\n  gdb> 42"]
[5.260759, "o", "\t    g.ring[slot] = payload;\r\n  gdb> $2 = 48\r\n  gdb> rax            0x40                64\r\n  gdb> Breakpoint 2 at 0x40000070: file user/laplace/heisenbug.c, line 36.\r\n  gdb> Thread 1 hit Breakpoint 2, produce (payload=payload@entry=40884, burst=burst@entry=1) at user/laplace/heisenbug.c:36\r\n  gdb> 36\t    if (burst) {\r\n  gdb> 0x00000000400001bc in main () at user/laplace/heisenbug.c:66\r\n  gdb> 66\t        produce(payload, burst);\r\n  gdb> => 0x400001bc <main+252>:\tcall   0x40000070 <produce>\r\n  gdb> byte-exact: 1 epochs re-executed from their keyframes\r\n  gdb> [Inferior 1 (Remote target) detached]\r\n  [ok] gdb reads the clobbered value\r\n  [ok] watch + reverse-continue: stopped where batch_limit was about to change from 48\r\n"]
[5.26122, "o", "  [ok]   ...inside produce(), during a burst, with the clobbering payload\r\n"]
[5.261499, "o", "  [ok]   ...with batch_limit still 48 and slot index rax = 64\r\n  [ok] break produce + reverse-continue stops in produce()\r\n"]
[5.261524, "o", "  [ok] monitor verify: byte-exact\r\n\r\n[mcp ] resume past the bug: the machine keeps running and recording\r\n"]
[5.265223, "o", "  mcp> list_checkpoints()\r\n       checkpoints: count=1 oldest=1 newest=1\r\n"]
[6.81341, "o", "  mcp> resume()\r\n       ran live and stopped at epoch=12 offset=4186 insn=0 pid=2 rip=0x4000003b stop=interrupt: a debugger asked to stop (end of the recording)\r\n  [ok] resumed live, then stopped by the next request\r\n  [ok] the interrupting request was answered\r\n"]
[6.855356, "o", "  mcp> list_checkpoints()\r\n       checkpoints: count=12 oldest=1 newest=12\r\n  [ok] the recording grew past the bug\r\n"]
[8.854351, "o", "  mcp> verify_replay()\r\n       byte-exact: epochs_checked=12 epochs_diverged=0\r\n  [ok] the extended recording re-executes byte-exact\r\n"]
[9.1322, "o", "PASSED: recorded a heisenbug in the booted OS and found the clobbering store backward, over MCP and gdb, with every reconstructed epoch byte-exact\r\n"]
